.TH UGPIBD-SCPI 1 "2026-08-01" "ugpibd 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ugpibd\-scpi \- interactive SCPI client for ugpibd over HiSLIP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ugpibd\-scpi
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ugpibd\-scpi
is a small REPL for talking to instruments through a running
.BR ugpibd (1).
It speaks HiSLIP, the same transport pyvisa uses, so it does not need the
Prologix front-end enabled.
.PP
Each input line is one request/response round-trip: a line containing
.B ?
is sent as a query and its reply printed; any other line is written without
reading a response. Non-TTY stdin is supported, so the client can be driven
from a pipe or a script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
Host running
.BR ugpibd .
Default
.IR localhost .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
HiSLIP port. Default
.IR 4880 .
.TP
.BI \-\-addr " PAD"
GPIB primary address to talk to, encoded as the HiSLIP sub-address
.I hislip<PAD>
at connect time. The address is fixed for the session. Omit to use the daemon's
default PAD.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit. The first line carries the version.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH META-COMMANDS
Lines beginning with
.B ++
are mapped to HiSLIP control operations rather than sent to the instrument.
.TP
.B ++clr
Selected Device Clear.
.TP
.B ++trg
GPIB trigger (GET).
.TP
.BI ++ren " 0|1"
Remote enable off or on.
.TP
.B ++status
Print the serial-poll status byte.
.TP
.B ++help
List the meta-commands.
.SH EXAMPLES
Query the instrument at GPIB primary address 15:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ugpibd\-scpi \-\-addr 15
.fi
.RE
.PP
Drive it from a pipe:
.PP
.RS
.nf
printf '++ren 1\\n*RST\\n*IDN?\\n' | ugpibd\-scpi \-\-addr 15
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ugpibd (1)
